<v Ira Glass>第三幕，“另一个现实世界”。你知道，当你创业时，它通常会占据你的生活，至少有一段时间。最后一个故事关于某个人全身心投入到一个商业计划中，而那实际上是一个持续终生的完整人生计划。这个故事是为名为《Love + Radio》的播客制作的。这个故事在很多方面都很不寻常，而且非常棒。故事中说话的女士名叫泰勒·罗斯·内申斯（Taylor Rose Nations）。这是泰勒。

00:41:15.580 --> 00:41:42.640
<v Taylor Rose Nations>When I was a nursing assistant, I took care of a lady who couldn't chew any food. Bad teeth, she didn't want to go get them pulled out-- she was so old. She just, like, was cool with drinking juice the rest of her life. And her family decided that it would be better for her to get her teeth pulled and get dentures. She ended up getting her teeth pulled. And after that, she refused to eat. And she ended up just dying.
<v Taylor Rose Nations>当我是护士助理时，我照顾过一位不能咀嚼任何食物的女士。牙齿很烂，她不想去拔掉——她太老了。她只是觉得余生喝果汁过日子也挺好。她的家人认为拔掉牙齿并装上假牙对她更好。最终她拔了牙。在那之后，她拒绝进食。结果她就那样死去了。

00:41:42.640 --> 00:42:00.720
<v Taylor Rose Nations>After somebody dies, we strip the bed, sanitize the room. It's this whole thing. And the next patient called me in and she asked me, "Did somebody just die in this bed?" And I said, "Uh, yeah. [LAUGHS] They did." And she said, "I thought so, because they just bit me."
<v Taylor Rose Nations>有人去世后，我们清理床铺，消毒房间。整套程序都是这样。下一位病人把我叫进去，问我：“这张床上刚才是不是有人去世了？”我说：“呃，是的。（笑）是的。”她说：“我想也是，因为他们刚才咬了我一口。”

00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:27.280
<v Taylor Rose Nations>And I was just like, what are you talking about? And she said, "Yeah, they just bit me, and I reached back to where they bit me and I found this." And it was a tooth, like a full tooth with, like, the roots and-- And I said, "Are you sure that's not your tooth?" And she was like, "I'm pretty sure I'd know if I lost a tooth."
<v Taylor Rose Nations>我当时就想，你在说什么？她说：“是的，他们刚才咬了我，我摸了摸被咬的地方，发现了这个。”那是一颗牙齿，就像一颗完整的牙齿，带有牙根——我问她：“你确定那不是你自己的牙吗？”她说：“如果我掉了一颗牙我肯定会知道。”

00:42:27.280 --> 00:42:57.840
<v Taylor Rose Nations>If I hadn't had those experiences, I would probably 100% say, like, you just die. You stop living. But who knows? I haven't died yet. I don't believe in, like, an afterlife in a biblical sense or anything like that. I kind of think you probably just stop being.
<v Taylor Rose Nations>如果我没有那些经历，我可能会 100% 说，人死了就只是死了。你停止了生活。但谁知道呢？我还没死过。我不相信圣经意义上的那种“来世”之类的东西。我有点认为你可能只是停止了存在。

00:42:57.840 --> 00:43:22.670
<v Taylor Rose Nations>I think there are probably a lot of things that I'll miss. My family, and books. Pizza, and beer, especially. If nobody's actually looked at the website, I think it kind of sounds crazy. I think most people think I'm, like, getting sucked into some weird cult.
<v Taylor Rose Nations>我想可能有很多我会错过的事情。我的家人，书。披萨和啤酒，尤其是。如果没人看过那个网站，我觉得这听起来很疯狂。我想大多数人都觉得我像被卷入了某个奇怪的邪教。

00:43:22.670 --> 00:43:44.060
<v Taylor Rose Nations>I literally never go to the doctor, so I was nervous anyway. Having to make that appointment kind of made this a little bit more real an experience. Vision test, colorblind, hearing, breathing, blood work, blood pressure. Then I had to have an EKG done. Pelvic exam.
<v Taylor Rose Nations>我几乎从不去医生那里，所以我本来就很紧张。必须预约体检让这件事变得更真实了一些。视力测试、色盲测试、听力、呼吸、验血、血压。然后我不得不做了心电图，还有盆腔检查。

